.TH SOCKETADDR 2N UniSoft
.SH NAME
socketaddr \- return address associated with a socket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <net/socket.h>
.sp
.B socketaddr(s, addr)
.br
.B int s;
.br
.B struct sockaddr *addr;
.SH DESCRIPTION
The address associated with the socket
.I s\^
is returned in
.IR addr .
If
.I s\^
is not a socket, \-1 is returned and an appropriate errno is
returned.
.SH SEE ALSO
socket(2N).
.SH BUGS
This call is provisional and will exist in a slightly different
form in future releases.
.\"N	 @(#)socketaddr.2N	 5.2 of 7/12/84
